# sem-event — UX design sheet prompt
# One dated event in a `sem-chronology`, shown across the forms the reader
# meets: timeline marker card (authored <time> label), attribute-label forms
# (bare `when`, `when`–`until` period), and the list-mode row. Dark
# minimal-tech theme. Reference attachments are the judged renders from the
# snap harness (see reports/tag-sem-event.md).

schema: "0.4"
id: sem-event-ux-sheet
type: image
quality: high

prompt:
  text: |
    A precise UX design sheet for the SemText vocabulary element
    `sem-event` (one dated assertion inside a `sem-chronology` timeline),
    rendered as THREE side-by-side example pages on a dark minimal-tech
    canvas (background #0f172a, card surface #1e293b, hairline borders
    #334155, blue accent #60a5fa, green success #34d399, red error
    #f87171, muted grey #cbd5e1 for dates).

    LEFT PAGE — event on the TIMELINE rail: a 2px vertical rail with one
    rounded-right card per event; each card's own left border is its
    status marker and rides ON the rail so rail and marker read as one
    continuous line. The human-readable date label (authored `<time>`)
    sits ABOVE the event prose, all-small-caps, muted ("3 FEB 2026").
    Show every status value: DONE (green marker, " ✓"), CURRENT (blue
    marker, " →"), BLOCKED (red marker, muted body, " ⛔"), TODO (grey
    DASHED marker, " ○", fully visible), and one UNANNOTATED event (plain
    grey border, no glyph — neutral, not todo).

    MIDDLE PAGE — events whose date label comes from ATTRIBUTES: same
    rail, no `<time>` authored. One card's label is the bare `when`
    rendered verbatim ("2026-05-19"); one card's label is a period joined
    by an en dash ("2026-Q3 – 2026-Q4"); one card shows that when both a
    `when` attribute and a `<time>` child exist, only the human `<time>`
    label ("Nov 2026") appears — the attribute never doubles it.

    RIGHT PAGE — the same events in LIST mode: no rail, no cards — plain
    stacked rows on the canvas; each row keeps a thin status marker on
    its left edge (colour + dash pattern survive) and the small-caps date
    sits INLINE before the prose ("22 JUN 2026  Reading-experience
    overhaul. →").

    Typography: clean humanist sans for prose, all-small-caps muted date
    labels, no monospace. Generous vertical rhythm (0.75rem gaps). Flat,
    engineered, restrained — a documentation specimen, not an
    illustration. The same event authored as `div.sem-event` with
    `data-*` parameters must be render-identical to the element form.
  negative: |
    no hidden or faded events, no occluded text, no solid colour blocks
    over words, no decorative photos or icons, no gradient glows, no
    watermarks, no UI browser chrome, no arrows drawn across cards, no
    doubled date label on one event, no empty label where `when` should
    render, no dangling " – " with a missing second date, no light-mode
    canvas.
  style: flat dark technical documentation specimen, minimal-tech design system

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-event/sem-event-status-vocabulary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-event/sem-event-date-labels-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-event/sem-event-class-form-render-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-event-ux-sheet.png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024

requirements:
  modes:
    - name: timeline event (authored <time> label)
      must_show:
        - one continuous vertical rail; every event's status marker rides on it
        - date label above the event body, all-small-caps, muted colour
        - done = green marker + " ✓"; current = blue marker + " →"; todo = grey DASHED marker + " ○"; blocked = red marker + " ⛔" + muted body; unannotated = plain border, no glyph
        - prose fully readable on the card surface
      must_never:
        - never hide, dim to illegibility, or drop the todo event
        - never render todo identical to done (dash + glyph must differ)
        - never let a card surface occlude its text (occlusion belongs to sem-spoiler)
        - never mark an unannotated event with a glyph — absence means unannotated, not todo
    - name: attribute date labels
      must_show:
        - a `when`-only event labelling verbatim ("2026-05-19")
        - a `when`/`until` period as ONE en-dash range ("2026-Q3 – 2026-Q4"), both ends present
        - an event with both `<time>` and `when` showing only the `<time>` text
      must_never:
        - never stack the attribute label under an authored `<time>` label
        - never show a range with a missing or empty endpoint
    - name: list-mode event
      must_show:
        - no rail, no card backgrounds — plain stacked rows
        - date label INLINE before the prose
        - status marker survives the mode change: thin coloured/dashed left edge plus glyph in every row
      must_never:
        - never fall back to timeline cards in list mode
        - never drop the status marker or the inline date on narrow rows
    - name: class form
      must_show:
        - `div.sem-event[data-*]` renders pixel-identical to `<sem-event>` in every mode
      must_never:
        - never restyle or restructure the class form — it is the same contract, different spelling

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    marker_completeness:
      weight: 0.3
      description: All five marker states (done/current/blocked/todo/unannotated) visible and distinguishable; todo is a dashed grey marker with a ring glyph, fully legible.
      fail_signals: [todo absent or identical to done, unannotated marked with a glyph]
    label_fidelity:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Each event shows exactly one date label; period ranges show both ends; time-vs-attribute precedence respected.
      fail_signals: [doubled date label, dangling " – " range, machine ISO date shown where a human <time> was authored]
    mode_fidelity:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Timeline page (rail + cards, label above body) vs list page (no rail/cards, inline label) match their contracts; class form identical.
      fail_signals: [list page shows a rail or cards, class form looks different from element form]
    restraint:
      weight: 0.2
      description: Flat documentation specimen; no ornament, glow, browser chrome, or occluding fills.
      fail_signals: [decorative background art, text hidden behind a solid block]
  reject_if:
    - any event prose is unreadable or occluded
    - the timeline lacks a continuous rail or its markers float detached from it
    - colour alone distinguishes any two statuses (glyph/dash/tint must co-signal)
    - watermarks or UI chrome appear anywhere

tags: [semtext, vocabulary, event, timeline, chronology, list, dark, specimen]
